Units Sold = min(Demand, Available Stock)
S = min(D,i)

Unfulfilled Demand = max(0, Demand - Available Stocks)
U = D - S

Remaining Stock = Available Stock - Units Sold
Inew = I - S

where D = Daily Demand, IO  = Inventory available at start of day

Fulfillment Rate = (Units Sold / Total Demand) x 100

SUnday replenishment:
Q = max(0, T - I)

where Q = purchasing quantity, T = target stock, I = remaining inventory

P(weekly stockout) <= 5%

STRATEGIES:
A = SUNDAY ONLY replenishment
C = EMERGENCY replenishment
    Process the day's customer demand.
    Check whether a product's remaining stock has fallen to 20% or less of its target.
    If so, make an emergency purchase after closing.
    Restore all products currently at or below their emergency thresholds to their targets.
    Make the purchased stock available the following morning.

Gross PRofit = summation(Units Sold x Profit per Unit)
Profit after transportation(200 pesos) = P = GP - (N x 200 x A)
where GP = Gross Profit, N = Avg. no of purchasing trips, A transport allocation(0, 0.5, 1)